WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.670
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:03.838
[gun cocks]

3
00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:08.007
Look. I don't want to. but...
it's just so much money.

4
00:00:08.092 --> 00:00:09.009
[woman] Money?

5
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:13.055
Come on. Corrigan. you don't honestly
think you'll get away with this.

6
00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:15.015
[chuckles] Oh. sure I will.

7
00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:17.184
[gunshot]

8
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.438
[gunshots continue]

9
00:00:20.521 --> 00:00:21.522
[woman] Barb.

10
00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:23.733
[yelling] Barb!

11
00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.777
-You okay?
-I'm fine. Renee.

12
00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:29.029
Just... distracted.

13
00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:31.657
-Are you sure that there's nothin'...
-I'm fine!

14
00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:35.828
[gunshots continue]

15
00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.747
[dramatic music continues]

16
00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:44.253
[theme music playing]

17
00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:16.494
[suspenseful music playing]

18
00:01:18.913 --> 00:01:20.914
[moody music playing]

19
00:01:22.041 --> 00:01:24.126
You seem a little... tense.

20
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.170
The guy who tried to murder me
is about to walk out of jail.

21
00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:28.714
So. sure. Just a little.

22
00:01:30.508 --> 00:01:32.176
Sorry.

23
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.594
I didn't mean to snap at you.

24
00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:36.764
What's this experiment he volunteered for
all about anyway?

25
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.642
I'll find out tonight at Blackgate.

26
00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:42.311
Barb. you're under no obligation
to be there.

27
00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:43.562
I have to.

28
00:01:43.646 --> 00:01:45.940
Jim Corrigan betrayed me. Renee.

29
00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:47.942
I have to look that animal
in the eyes and...

30
00:01:48.025 --> 00:01:51.237
And... you won't do it alone.

31
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.322
[dramatic music playing]

32
00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.579
[gate unlocks. opens]

33
00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:03.457
-[prison guard] Ready. Corrigan?
-No.

34
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:06.043
But let's do it.

35
00:02:11.966 --> 00:02:14.927
Who'd ya rat out to get
special treatment. Corrigan?

36
00:02:16.554 --> 00:02:18.806
-Miserable son of a--
-Shut up!

37
00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:22.560
[dramatic music continues]

38
00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:27.189
[doors creak open]

39
00:02:39.201 --> 00:02:43.079
[grunts] Hey. hey! Take it easy. fellas.

40
00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:47.293
Good evening. ladies.

41
00:02:48.502 --> 00:02:50.254
What are you doing here. Wayne?

42
00:02:50.337 --> 00:02:53.591
My people told me Dr. Peterson's
longevity experiments

43
00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:55.509
might be worth investing in.

44
00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:58.137
It's all about the money with you.
isn't it?

45
00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.847
What else is there?

46
00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.725
Well. aside from wine. women.
and the occasional song?

47
00:03:03.726 --> 00:03:04.560
Ladies.

48
00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:08.063
[both] I can't stand him.

49
00:03:08.898 --> 00:03:13.277
I'm Doctor James Peterson.
Head of the Osiris Project.

50
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.197
Tonight. my friends. we stand
at the gateway to a new age.

51
00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:19.867
where the recently deceased
may be resurrected.

52
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.453
And their lives extended by decades.

53
00:03:22.536 --> 00:03:27.708
And we thank Mr. Corrigan for volunteering
to be our first test subject.

54
00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:31.211
[scoffs] For volunteering
to have his sentence reduced.

55
00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:32.755
[machine beeping steadily]

56
00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:36.133
First. we must stop
the test subject's heart.

57
00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:38.719
[groaning]

58
00:03:38.802 --> 00:03:40.387
[suspenseful music playing]

59
00:03:40.471 --> 00:03:42.473
[beeping continues]

60
00:03:54.485 --> 00:03:57.488
[gasps. exhales]

61
00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:59.573
[watch ticking]

62
00:04:00.824 --> 00:04:02.826
[beeping continues]

63
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.872
[suspenseful music continues]

64
00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.130
[beeping decreasing]

65
00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.853
[sustained beep]

66
00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.939
[ticking continues]

67
00:04:33.524 --> 00:04:35.109
[beeping stops]

68
00:04:43.075 --> 00:04:44.576
-[clicking]
-[machine whirring]

69
00:04:44.659 --> 00:04:45.953
[buzzing]

70
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.415
[dramatic music playing]

71
00:04:50.499 --> 00:04:51.667
[whirring intensifies]

72
00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:02.928
[electricity charging up]

73
00:05:03.012 --> 00:05:04.888
[beeping]

74
00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:06.807
[pained screaming]

75
00:05:07.558 --> 00:05:10.310
-[beeping increasing]
-[electrical shocks]

76
00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:12.479
[screaming continues]

77
00:05:16.984 --> 00:05:19.486
[screaming intensifies]

78
00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.324
[electricity powers down]

79
00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.746
[music intensifies]

80
00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:46.513
He's dead?

81
00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:08.952
Corrigan's dead! He's dead!

82
00:06:09.036 --> 00:06:11.747
If they'll kill a cop.
they'll kill any of us!

83
00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.874
We're just lab animals to 'em!

84
00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:16.668
-[prisoners yelling]
-[gasping]

85
00:06:16.752 --> 00:06:19.463
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[grunting]

86
00:06:22.174 --> 00:06:24.259
[yelling continues]

87
00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:28.806
[gasps]

88
00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:35.437
[alarm ringing]

89
00:06:35.521 --> 00:06:36.814
[all] Hmm?

90
00:06:38.607 --> 00:06:39.691
Ladies.

91
00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.068
[gasps]

92
00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:43.570
If it's a prison break.
I gotta get you outta here.

93
00:06:43.654 --> 00:06:45.239
I can take care of myself.

94
00:06:45.322 --> 00:06:47.491
Yeah. maybe.
But if those prisoners find out

95
00:06:47.574 --> 00:06:50.619
the police commissioner's daughter's
in here... Let's go.

96
00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:54.039
[suspenseful music continues]

97
00:06:54.123 --> 00:06:55.082
[alarm blaring]

98
00:06:55.165 --> 00:06:58.544
Let me go! Please!
I've got a wife and kids!

99
00:06:58.627 --> 00:07:00.754
Not such a tough guy anymore. huh?

100
00:07:00.838 --> 00:07:02.798
[blaring continues]

101
00:07:02.881 --> 00:07:04.967
[dramatic music playing]

102
00:07:07.678 --> 00:07:08.804
[gate buzzing]

103
00:07:09.763 --> 00:07:11.348
[music intensifying]

104
00:07:14.268 --> 00:07:15.686
[yells. grunts]

105
00:07:16.186 --> 00:07:17.020
[grunts]

106
00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:18.856
[groans]

107
00:07:18.939 --> 00:07:20.774
[fighting grunts and groans]

108
00:07:24.778 --> 00:07:26.155
[dramatic music continues]

109
00:07:29.366 --> 00:07:30.325
[pained yells]

110
00:07:31.618 --> 00:07:32.786
[groans]

111
00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:45.174
-[moody music playing]
-[car driving]

112
00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:50.512
Hell of a way to die...
and it's almost Christmas.

113
00:07:50.596 --> 00:07:53.056
Hate to feel sorry for a guy
like Corrigan. but...

114
00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:56.393
[driver] Yeah. nobody should have
to go out like that.

115
00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.187
[suspenseful music playing]

116
00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.272
[man] So what are you doin'
for New Year's?

117
00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:02.482
[driver sighs]
Anything like last New Year's.

118
00:08:02.566 --> 00:08:05.319
I'll be trying to walk off
a wicked hangover from--

119
00:08:05.402 --> 00:08:06.278
[both gasp]

120
00:08:06.361 --> 00:08:07.905
-[shrieks]
-[tires screeching]

121
00:08:07.988 --> 00:08:09.489
[screaming]

122
00:08:09.573 --> 00:08:11.116
[crashes]

123
00:08:12.326 --> 00:08:13.952
[dramatic music playing]

124
00:08:14.036 --> 00:08:16.914
[Alfred] Perhaps it's a blessing
the experiment failed.

125
00:08:16.997 --> 00:08:20.500
We're not the most...
responsible species.

126
00:08:20.584 --> 00:08:23.962
And the power to extend
a lifespan indefinitely?

127
00:08:24.046 --> 00:08:26.298
Who decides how to use that? Who's--

128
00:08:26.381 --> 00:08:29.092
But think what a man could accomplish
if he had the time.

129
00:08:29.176 --> 00:08:31.178
-[Alfred] Sir?
-Nothing.

130
00:08:32.679 --> 00:08:34.556
In the spirit of the season. sir.

131
00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:38.894
I was thinking of baking the holiday
biscuits you so enjoyed as a boy.

132
00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:41.897
I remember how you
and your mother would--

133
00:08:42.898 --> 00:08:44.900
[dramatic music continues]

134
00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:47.527
[music sting]

135
00:08:47.611 --> 00:08:51.198
-[brakes screech]
-Ooh. Excuse the jolt. sir.

136
00:08:51.281 --> 00:08:53.283
It appears there's been an accident.

137
00:08:55.369 --> 00:08:57.371
[tense music playing]

138
00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.678
[dramatic music playing]

139
00:09:17.266 --> 00:09:19.810
[Gordon] You shouldn't have been there
in the first place.

140
00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:21.728
[Barbara] I had to face him. Dad.

141
00:09:21.812 --> 00:09:25.023
-You could've been killed.
-But I wasn't. was I?

142
00:09:25.107 --> 00:09:28.694
I've. uh... got some paperwork
to take care of.

143
00:09:28.777 --> 00:09:30.070
You do that.

144
00:09:30.779 --> 00:09:33.532
[sighs] Thank you. Renee.

145
00:09:36.535 --> 00:09:38.036
I'm okay. Dad.

146
00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.371
But...

147
00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:41.248
He died. Dad.

148
00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:42.708
A man died.

149
00:09:43.542 --> 00:09:45.669
And do you know how I felt?

150
00:09:46.336 --> 00:09:49.131
Relieved. [stumbles]
Maybe even happy.

151
00:09:50.215 --> 00:09:51.883
What does that say about me?

152
00:09:52.301 --> 00:09:55.595
It says you've been through
something traumatic. sweetheart.

153
00:09:56.638 --> 00:09:58.140
It says you're human.

154
00:09:59.057 --> 00:10:01.560
Why doesn't that make me feel any better?

155
00:10:02.394 --> 00:10:04.146
I'm gonna head home. Coming?

156
00:10:04.229 --> 00:10:07.566
I'd love to. but I've still got work
to finish up.

157
00:10:08.442 --> 00:10:11.278
Be careful out there. Barb.
Storm's getting rough.

158
00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:14.281
Oh please. I'm a better driver
than you are.

159
00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:16.575
I'll be careful.

160
00:10:20.287 --> 00:10:21.580
[jazzy music playing]

161
00:10:21.663 --> 00:10:23.206
[man] C'mon. Vinny. wrap it up.

162
00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.250
[Vinny] Another.

163
00:10:25.334 --> 00:10:28.045
No. Sorry. pally. I gotta get home to--

164
00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.839
[slurring] I said gimme another...

165
00:10:30.922 --> 00:10:32.424
"pally."

166
00:10:32.507 --> 00:10:35.552
All right. all right. Calm down. Stay.

167
00:10:36.053 --> 00:10:38.055
Stay as long as you'd like.

168
00:10:41.224 --> 00:10:43.226
[suspenseful music playing]

169
00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.187
[door creaks open]

170
00:10:56.323 --> 00:10:57.657
[music intensifies]

171
00:10:57.741 --> 00:10:59.284
[gasps]

172
00:10:59.368 --> 00:11:01.370
[belabored] Vinny...

173
00:11:02.329 --> 00:11:03.997
DeLeon.

174
00:11:05.332 --> 00:11:07.918
Corrigan? Is that you?

175
00:11:09.836 --> 00:11:11.296
Whaddya want?

176
00:11:12.798 --> 00:11:14.758
Vengeance.

177
00:11:14.841 --> 00:11:16.259
[intense music playing]

178
00:11:21.932 --> 00:11:23.183
[high-pitched ringing]

179
00:11:23.266 --> 00:11:25.685
-[heart pounding]
-[gasping in pain]

180
00:11:30.148 --> 00:11:32.317
[groaning. gasps]

181
00:11:32.401 --> 00:11:33.568
[thuds]

182
00:11:33.652 --> 00:11:36.113
[dramatic music playing]

183
00:11:46.331 --> 00:11:49.876
-You're sure that was his name?
-Oh. yeah. Called him Corrigan.

184
00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.671
Took one look at that guy.
and he caught a grabber.

185
00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.714
And Corrigan?

186
00:11:54.798 --> 00:11:58.552
Left with two bullets in him.
But I gotta tell ya...

187
00:11:58.635 --> 00:12:01.054
I can understand
why Vinny croaked like that.

188
00:12:01.138 --> 00:12:04.307
That Corrigan guy...
He didn't seem human.

189
00:12:06.685 --> 00:12:10.564
[man. over radio] Good evening. This is
Houseman Welch welcoming you

190
00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:15.068
to a special Christmas edition
of the Hermes Theater.

191
00:12:15.152 --> 00:12:18.947
Tonight. as I do every year
at this festive time.

192
00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.907
your obedient servant will be reading

193
00:12:20.991 --> 00:12:27.372
from Charles Dickens’ immortal tale
of redemption. A Christmas Carol.

194
00:12:27.456 --> 00:12:31.418
But first. a word from our friends
at the Conway Soup Company.

195
00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:32.836
[radio clicks off]

196
00:12:34.379 --> 00:12:36.298
[dramatic music playing]

197
00:12:40.844 --> 00:12:42.512
-[loud bang]
-[startled gasp]

198
00:12:44.264 --> 00:12:45.515
-[bang]
-[startled gasp]

199
00:12:46.349 --> 00:12:48.101
[creaking]

200
00:12:48.185 --> 00:12:50.395
Not tonight. Jacob Marley.

201
00:12:50.479 --> 00:12:51.688
[bang]

202
00:12:53.732 --> 00:12:54.983
-[grunts]
-[groans]

203
00:12:55.066 --> 00:12:57.194
I've just about had it with you!

204
00:12:57.277 --> 00:13:00.405
Please. Roger!
Please don't hurt me anymore. [groans]

205
00:13:00.989 --> 00:13:03.617
-I'm just getting started.
-[snow crunches]

206
00:13:04.993 --> 00:13:06.578
[suspenseful music playing]

207
00:13:12.501 --> 00:13:16.379
[belabored] Roger... Marshall.

208
00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:19.925
Corrigan?!

209
00:13:20.759 --> 00:13:22.177
[grunting and panting]

210
00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.262
[suspenseful music continues]

211
00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:29.100
[panting]

212
00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.105
[grunts]

213
00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:36.274
[groans]

214
00:13:38.276 --> 00:13:39.444
[panting]

215
00:13:39.528 --> 00:13:41.154
[groaning and panting]

216
00:13:46.701 --> 00:13:48.703
[dispatcher] Possible break-in
at Bergduff’s Department store.

217
00:13:48.787 --> 00:13:50.413
34th and O’Neil.

218
00:13:50.497 --> 00:13:54.793
Two men spotted in the area. and. uh.
witness claims one of 'em's a zombie.

219
00:13:54.876 --> 00:13:57.379
-[tires screech]
-[suspenseful music playing]

220
00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:59.464
[panting]

221
00:14:02.259 --> 00:14:03.802
[shrieks. groans]

222
00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:05.470
[groaning and panting]

223
00:14:07.931 --> 00:14:09.683
He's gone.

224
00:14:09.766 --> 00:14:10.934
[chuckling]

225
00:14:11.017 --> 00:14:14.396
I'm safe. I'm safe. and he can't get in--

226
00:14:14.479 --> 00:14:15.605
[gasps]

227
00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.441
What do you want from me. Corrigan?

228
00:14:20.151 --> 00:14:22.404
Vengeance.

229
00:14:24.739 --> 00:14:26.741
You're here about Veronica?

230
00:14:27.576 --> 00:14:29.786
Uh. listen... [sputters]

231
00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:36.293
That wasn't on me! She was my wife!
She fell down those stairs! The jury said!

232
00:14:36.376 --> 00:14:37.544
Come on. brother.

233
00:14:37.627 --> 00:14:40.171
You're not gonna ice me
over one worthless piece--

234
00:14:40.255 --> 00:14:42.132
[grunts. groans]

235
00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:43.174
[growls]

236
00:14:44.217 --> 00:14:46.094
[groaning and panting]

237
00:14:47.137 --> 00:14:48.763
-[chuckles. laughs]
-[distant music]

238
00:14:48.847 --> 00:14:50.807
-[engine revving]
-[shrieking]

239
00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:53.059
-[bones crunching]
-[brakes slam]

240
00:14:53.143 --> 00:14:55.770
[gasps and grunts]

241
00:14:55.854 --> 00:14:58.398
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

242
00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:01.526
[dramatic music playing]

243
00:15:17.334 --> 00:15:19.336
[phone ringing]

244
00:15:20.045 --> 00:15:21.546
-Hello?
-[Gordon] It's Dad.

245
00:15:22.213 --> 00:15:24.341
Looks like I'll be later than expected.

246
00:15:24.424 --> 00:15:27.510
I swear Christmas Eve's
just like a full moon in this town.

247
00:15:27.594 --> 00:15:29.596
All the loonies come out.

248
00:15:29.679 --> 00:15:30.972
[Barbara] Should I wait up?

249
00:15:31.056 --> 00:15:33.767
[Gordon] You don't have to sweetheart.
I'll see you in the morning.

250
00:15:35.352 --> 00:15:39.814
-Are you okay? You sound...
-No. no. I'm fine.

251
00:15:39.898 --> 00:15:40.732
It's just...

252
00:15:41.441 --> 00:15:43.735
I can't get Corrigan out of my head.

253
00:15:43.818 --> 00:15:46.738
The sound of him screaming.
his body writhing in pain. I...

254
00:15:46.821 --> 00:15:50.950
Forget Corrigan.
He did what he did and paid for it.

255
00:15:51.826 --> 00:15:54.913
[Gordon] You are here. Alive and well.

256
00:15:55.789 --> 00:15:56.790
Justice.

257
00:15:57.957 --> 00:15:59.542
That's my early Christmas present.

258
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.798
I left you some of my traditional eggnog
in the fridge.

259
00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:06.800
Your eggnog is awful. Dad.

260
00:16:07.384 --> 00:16:10.845
And that's part of the tradition.
[chuckles]

261
00:16:10.929 --> 00:16:12.097
I'll see you soon.

262
00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:13.848
[phone clatters]

263
00:16:13.932 --> 00:16:16.893
[dramatic music playing]

264
00:16:19.729 --> 00:16:21.731
[dispatcher] Looks like our zombie's
been spotted again.

265
00:16:21.815 --> 00:16:24.150
Sixth and 51st near Wycliffe Center.

266
00:16:26.319 --> 00:16:28.446
[Welch. over radio]
"Then he heard the noise much louder.

267
00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:32.117
on the floors below.
then coming up the stairs.

268
00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.869
then coming straight towards his door!

269
00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:37.789
It came on through the heavy door..."

270
00:16:37.872 --> 00:16:39.833
Geez. late again.

271
00:16:39.915 --> 00:16:41.793
Considering what I pay that broad...

272
00:16:41.876 --> 00:16:43.670
-You'd think she'd be a--
-[knocking]

273
00:16:43.753 --> 00:16:45.672
-[on radio] "Who are you?"
-Get that.

274
00:16:45.755 --> 00:16:47.882
[suspenseful music playing]

275
00:16:47.966 --> 00:16:51.720
[on radio] "'Who were you then?'
said Scrooge. raising his voice."

276
00:16:53.179 --> 00:16:55.098
[ominous music playing]

277
00:16:55.181 --> 00:16:59.269
Freddy... Borke.

278
00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:03.648
Corrigan? But... but word
from my boys is you're dead!

279
00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.112
[grunts. struggling]

280
00:17:09.738 --> 00:17:11.030
[neck cracks]

281
00:17:11.114 --> 00:17:12.531
[grunts]

282
00:17:12.615 --> 00:17:13.657
[groans]

283
00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:18.079
[gasps. pants]
What do you want from me?

284
00:17:18.163 --> 00:17:21.040
Vengeance.

285
00:17:21.124 --> 00:17:22.541
[music intensifies]

286
00:17:22.625 --> 00:17:24.586
[grunts. groans]

287
00:17:24.669 --> 00:17:25.627
[panting]

288
00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:29.424
[grunts and pants]

289
00:17:36.014 --> 00:17:37.098
[whimpers]

290
00:17:37.599 --> 00:17:39.392
[engine revs]

291
00:17:39.476 --> 00:17:41.227
[tires screech]

292
00:17:41.936 --> 00:17:45.356
-[pants and grunts]
-[suspenseful music continues]

293
00:17:51.613 --> 00:17:53.865
Oh! No!

294
00:17:53.948 --> 00:17:56.409
Not you too! [gasps]

295
00:17:57.243 --> 00:17:59.621
[grunting]

296
00:18:01.498 --> 00:18:02.707
[groans]

297
00:18:02.791 --> 00:18:04.125
[rattling]

298
00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.088
[high-pitched ringing]

299
00:18:09.547 --> 00:18:12.300
[suspenseful music playing]

300
00:18:18.306 --> 00:18:20.475
[panting]

301
00:18:22.227 --> 00:18:23.478
[groans]

302
00:18:23.895 --> 00:18:25.271
[high-pitched ringing]

303
00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:26.523
[gasps]

304
00:18:26.606 --> 00:18:27.899
[pants and grunts]

305
00:18:31.194 --> 00:18:33.655
-[music intensifies]
-[struggling]

306
00:18:36.449 --> 00:18:39.410
[screams]

307
00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.622
[shrieks. whimpers

308
00:18:43.456 --> 00:18:44.374
[snaps]

309
00:18:44.457 --> 00:18:46.876
[screaming]

310
00:18:49.003 --> 00:18:50.713
-[stabbing sound]
-[crowd screaming]

311
00:18:50.797 --> 00:18:52.924
[dramatic music playing]

312
00:18:58.137 --> 00:19:00.139
[ominous music playing]

313
00:19:09.232 --> 00:19:11.234
[phone ringing]

314
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.236
Dad?

315
00:19:13.319 --> 00:19:16.197
[Batman] Vinny DeLeon. Roger Marshall.
Freddy Borke.

316
00:19:16.281 --> 00:19:17.115
Batman.

317
00:19:17.198 --> 00:19:19.701
I need to know how they're connected
to Jim Corrigan.

318
00:19:19.784 --> 00:19:22.912
-[Barbara] Corrigan? Corrigan's dead.
-I beg to differ.

319
00:19:22.996 --> 00:19:24.163
He's alive?

320
00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:29.961
-Peterson's experiment. It must've...
-What do these three men have in common?

321
00:19:32.297 --> 00:19:33.506
DeLeon. he...

322
00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:36.092
[Batman] Bilked dozens of people
out of their life savings.

323
00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:37.677
Marshall murdered his wife.

324
00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.971
Borke had his fingers
deep in the drug trade.

325
00:19:40.054 --> 00:19:42.473
I know all that. What's the connection?

326
00:19:43.892 --> 00:19:46.769
Corrigan was the arresting officer
in all three cases.

327
00:19:46.853 --> 00:19:48.396
[Batman] And?

328
00:19:49.606 --> 00:19:51.649
There wasn't sufficient
evidence to convict.

329
00:19:51.733 --> 00:19:53.693
So it's unfinished business.

330
00:19:53.776 --> 00:19:55.778
Hooking the fish that got away.

331
00:19:56.404 --> 00:19:58.156
You got away too. Barbara.

332
00:19:58.239 --> 00:19:59.699
What? No.

333
00:20:00.283 --> 00:20:03.578
There's no reward anymore.
He has no earthly reason to--

334
00:20:03.661 --> 00:20:07.290
We don't know what he's thinking.
Call your father. Get protection.

335
00:20:07.373 --> 00:20:09.459
-If he is coming for you. then--
-[hangs up]

336
00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:15.506
Then I'll be ready.

337
00:20:16.591 --> 00:20:19.093
-[dramatic music playing]
-[people screaming]

338
00:20:19.177 --> 00:20:21.346
[tires screeching]

339
00:20:21.429 --> 00:20:23.097
[screaming continues]

340
00:20:26.225 --> 00:20:28.144
[dramatic music continues]

341
00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.526
Corrigan.

342
00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.115
[fighting grunts and groans]

343
00:20:45.119 --> 00:20:47.205
[heavy breathing]

344
00:20:48.539 --> 00:20:51.084
[grunts and groans continue]

345
00:20:58.716 --> 00:21:00.343
[exciting music playing]

346
00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:19.988
[heavy breathing. groans]

347
00:21:20.738 --> 00:21:21.656
[groans]

348
00:21:22.156 --> 00:21:25.118
-[cracking]
-[pained grunts]

349
00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.205
[groans]

350
00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:31.290
[tracks squeaking]

351
00:21:34.919 --> 00:21:38.589
[dramatic music playing]

352
00:21:58.568 --> 00:22:01.821
[suspenseful music playing]

353
00:22:09.412 --> 00:22:12.290
Time to end this.
One way or another.

354
00:22:14.208 --> 00:22:16.044
[suspenseful music continues]

355
00:22:21.799 --> 00:22:23.801
[belabored breathing]

356
00:22:25.261 --> 00:22:28.097
[pants and groans]

357
00:22:28.181 --> 00:22:31.309
[Corrigan groaning] Barbara...

358
00:22:32.185 --> 00:22:34.187
Gordon.

359
00:22:35.313 --> 00:22:37.398
Not another step.

360
00:22:46.741 --> 00:22:49.535
Ready to die again? You son of a bitch.

361
00:22:56.125 --> 00:22:57.668
Barbara.

362
00:23:11.307 --> 00:23:12.934
I never hurt you!

363
00:23:13.017 --> 00:23:15.186
I'm not some criminal who escaped justice!

364
00:23:15.269 --> 00:23:17.980
You tried to kill me. For money!

365
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:20.566
So why. Jim? Why are you here?

366
00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:23.152
What do you want from me?

367
00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.782
[belabored] Forgiveness.

368
00:23:27.865 --> 00:23:30.368
[pained panting]

369
00:23:31.327 --> 00:23:33.746
[groaning. gasping]

370
00:23:38.501 --> 00:23:39.961
[shivering] Please.

371
00:23:40.837 --> 00:23:42.588
Forgive me.

372
00:23:44.215 --> 00:23:46.008
[wind blowing]

373
00:23:48.803 --> 00:23:50.179
[grunting]

374
00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:55.560
Barbara!

375
00:24:03.401 --> 00:24:06.320
[gasps. groans]

376
00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:19.083
Dead.

377
00:24:20.418 --> 00:24:21.836
He's dead.

378
00:24:21.919 --> 00:24:23.754
He came all this way and...

379
00:24:24.547 --> 00:24:26.841
He just wanted me to forgive him.

380
00:24:29.135 --> 00:24:30.511
That's all.

381
00:24:31.679 --> 00:24:35.183
[emotional music playing]

382
00:24:44.025 --> 00:24:46.027
[distant sirens]

383
00:24:50.823 --> 00:24:52.700
[brakes screeching]

384
00:25:01.667 --> 00:25:03.044
You all right?

385
00:25:03.127 --> 00:25:04.462
[sighs] Honestly?

386
00:25:05.421 --> 00:25:06.422
No.

387
00:25:10.801 --> 00:25:14.347
But... I think I will be.

388
00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:16.432
[emotional music continues]

389
00:25:21.062 --> 00:25:24.815
-[engine revs]
-[brakes screech]

390
00:25:30.404 --> 00:25:32.406
[melancholy music playing]

391
00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:47.004
[credits music playing]
